{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>For with a strong hand.</b> When prophecy strengthened itself upon me, as \"the hand of YHWH was upon me\" (Ezekiel 37:1):" "<b>And He instructed me.</b> The samekh has a dagesh to compensate for the elision of the yod, which is the first root letter, like \"Before I formed you in the womb\" (Jeremiah 1:8). And so ויסרני demonstrates the correctness of my interpretation of the phrase טמא שפתים (Isaiah 6:5)."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {1 "The dagesh in the samekh of ויסרני compensates for the dropped first radical yod; Ibn Ezra cites this form to support his reading of Isaiah 6:5."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:52:49.185164665Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}